This product depends on, and adapts ideas from, the following Apache-2.0 projects:

- openWakeWord (David Scripka): feature front end, streaming runtime and precomputed
  ACAV100M/validation features. https://github.com/dscripka/openWakeWord
- livekit-wakeword (LiveKit): conv-attention classifier, focal-loss training schedule
  and the Piper VITS sample generator. https://github.com/livekit/livekit-wakeword
- Kokoro-82M (hexgrad): text-to-speech model and voices. https://huggingface.co/hexgrad/Kokoro-82M


Further models and datasets are downloaded at run time and remain under their own terms:
VoxCPM2 (OpenBMB), Whisper large-v3-turbo (OpenAI), Piper LibriTTS voice (Rhasspy),
MUSAN (OpenSLR), MIT environmental impulse responses, Multilingual LibriSpeech (Meta)
and ACAV100M-derived features. Check each licence before distributing trained models
for commercial use.
